/F1 8 Tf
11 TL
48 752 Td
(# Codex Workbench: daily commands) Tj
T*
(Ubuntu add-on for project setup, native session resume and scoped policy updates.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(ACTIVATE in an already-open Bash terminal \(new terminals load this automatically\)) Tj
T*
(  source ~/.local/share/codex-code/code-shell.bash) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(START WORK) Tj
T*
(  codex --code                         Start with the Workbench baseline) Tj
T*
(  cx "your task"                       Same workflow, with an initial task) Tj
T*
(  cx --one-off "small experiment"      Disposable work without project ceremony) Tj
T*
(Quick tasks stay quick. Existing projects keep their conventions. Substantial work) Tj
T*
(loads only relevant lifecycle guidance. Plain codex retains normal behavior.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(FIND / RESUME SESSIONS) Tj
T*
(  codex -cr                            All-directory native picker on this host) Tj
T*
(  codex --coderesume                   Same as -cr; cxr is also an alias) Tj
T*
(  cxr --last                           Latest native session across directories) Tj
T*
(  codex -cr --host HOST                Picker on an SSH-accessible host) Tj
T*
(  codex -cr --host HOST THREAD_UUID    Continue that original native thread) Tj
T*
(Workbench resume uses the saved session directory. SSH keeps work on that host.) Tj
T*
(Shared project files alone) Tj
T*
(do not migrate conversation history, credentials, memory or running processes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(UPGRADE EXISTING CODE-MODE SESSIONS) Tj
T*
(  codex --code --upgrade               Choose, apply and queue a relevance review) Tj
T*
(  codex --code --upgrade --preview) Tj
T*
(                                       Choose a session for a read-only preview) Tj
T*
(In the menu: /words searches, a number or exact ID selects, q cancels.) Tj
T*
(For scripts: add --thread THREAD_UUID. Add --host HOST to target another host.) Tj
T*
(  codex --code --upgrade --thread THREAD_UUID --check) Tj
T*
(Only an agent's acknowledgement confirms its review. It records applicable,) Tj
T*
(skipped or conflicting rules, preserving the task, history and local requirements.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(INSTALL / UPDATE THE ADD-ON \(Codex is installed/authenticated separately\)) Tj
T*
(  python3 workflow/install-portable.py --project-root /mnt/s/code --chrome off) Tj
T*
(Review the preview, then repeat with --apply. Missing external storage is refused.) Tj
T*
(Python 3.10+; existing tomli helps configuration inventory on Python 3.10.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(REMOTE CONTROL / KNOWLEDGE) Tj
T*
(  systemctl --user status codex-code-remote-control.timer) Tj
T*
(  python3 ~/.local/share/codex-code/coordinator.py probe) Tj
T*
(  python3 ~/.local/share/codex-code/coordinator.py search "topic") Tj
T*
(Remote-control recovery is enabled by default; pairing may require account setup.) Tj
T*
(KB uses each host's existing scoped identity. Vault access awaits separate rollout.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(CLAUDE \(OPTIONAL: install with --with-claude\)) Tj
T*
(  claude --code "task"                 Shared baseline, native Claude permissions) Tj
T*
(  claude --resume                      All-project metadata menu; native fallback) Tj
T*
(  claude --code --upgrade              Choose registered Claude policy updates) Tj
T*
(Native fallback: command claude --resume, then Ctrl+A for all projects and search.) Tj
T*
(Existing Claude chats require an explicit policy read; provider histories stay native.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(FILES / LIMITS) Tj
T*
(Installed helpers: ~/.local/share/codex-code/   Settings: ~/.config/codex-code/) Tj
T*
(Stable sessions: ~/.local/share/codex-work/sessions/   Project files: /mnt/s/code/) Tj
T*
(Policy snapshots and receipts stay in the selected session's workbench/ directory.) Tj
T*
(Source/docs: github.com/dblagbro/CodexWorkbench | docs/commands-and-installation.md) Tj
T*
(Reboot session restoration, execution-host migration and full vault access are pending.) Tj
T*
ET
